## Everything a developer portal needs

{% card-grid %}
{% card title="Interactive API reference" icon="code" href="/docs/api-reference/reference-pages" %}
Every OpenAPI 3.0, 3.1 or Swagger 2.0 spec gets a reference page rendered by RapiDoc, with Try, code samples and a sidebar that stays in view.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Guides as code" icon="book-open" href="/docs/writing/markdown" %}
Markdown, MDX and Markdoc pages in a `docs/` folder. Callouts, tabs, steps, cards, and live API operations inside a guide.
{% /card %}
{% card title="One config file" icon="sliders-horizontal" href="/docs/configuration/overview" %}
`rapidoc.config.yaml` describes the header, tabs, sidebars, theme and footer. A strict schema names every typo.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Search built in" icon="magnifying-glass" href="/docs/configuration/docs-search-redirects" %}
Full-text search across guides and API operations, indexed at build time. No search service to run.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Sign-in and access rules" icon="lock" href="/docs/access/overview" %}
Optional OpenID Connect sign-in. Decide who may read which pages, APIs and files, by group or email.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Mock server" icon="test-tube" href="/docs/tools/mock-server" %}
Serve your specs with their examples, validate requests, and check real OAuth scopes, so Try works before the API does.
{% /card %}
{% /card-grid %}

## From zero to portal

```bash
npm create rapidoc@latest my-portal
cd my-portal
npm run dev
```

The starter finds the OpenAPI files already in the folder, writes a `rapidoc.config.yaml` and a first guide, and opens the portal on `http://localhost:4321`. [Read the quickstart](/docs/getting-started/quickstart/).

## A live operation, right in a guide

Guides can embed any operation from your specs. This one comes from the [example Bookstore API](/apis/bookstore/). Run `npm run mock` in this site's repository and **Try** answers from the mock server.

{% api-operation spec="bookstore" path="/books" method="get" /%}

{% callout type="rocket" title="Moving from Zudoku or Redocly?" %}
`rapidoc migrate --from zudoku` or `--from redocly` writes a `rapidoc.config.yaml` from your existing project. [See migrating](/docs/tools/migrate/).
{% /callout %}
